                {
                  "type": "textComponent",
                  "text": "Using pressure plate data from the gait lab I used three different methods to characterise foot shape in order to differentiate between normal and flat footed patients. The three methods tested were the position of the centre of pressure of the foot during gait, fourier series to quantify shape and principal component analyses using sliding landmarks. These methods were carried out using Matlab code that I had written."
